[en.FOCUS_C18_101_CIVIL_RESEARCH]
Backward Advantage

[en.FOCUS_C18_101_CIVIL_RESEARCH_desc]
Compared to large cities like Las Pegasus, Manehattan, and Canterlot, our industrialization has just begun, or even has not reached the starting line. But this means that we can “cross the Stream of Silence by touching the previous Nirik”. We can avoid the mistakes made by those cities in the industrialization process, and directly use their experience and technology.

[zh.FOCUS_C18_101_CIVIL_RESEARCH]
后发优势

[zh.FOCUS_C18_101_CIVIL_RESEARCH_desc]
相比于洛马基、马哈顿、坎特洛特等大城市，我们的工业化才刚刚起步，或者说连起步标准都没有达到。但这恰恰意味着我们可以“摸着上一只逆麟过静默溪”，避免那些城市在工业化过程中犯下的错误，直接拿来他们的经验和技术。

